7 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566192 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fc24bef0-f8cf-5321-9a6d-d5127a9ed564" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566200 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566200 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61687" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566200 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566200 #edb/ref 1071 "A radioactive substance decays exponentially such that its mass reduces by $\\frac{1}{4}$ every hour. If the mass of the substance was initially $2\\,\\text{kg},$ what is the mass of the substance after $9$ hours?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566200 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "09a2f783-f81f-5ba2-8e8b-78ad6330c2dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566200 #edb/ref 1074 "If the mass reduces by $\\frac{1}{4},$ then $\\frac{3}{4}$ of its mass remains every hour.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ hour, the mass is $2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{4}).$\n\n- After $2$ hours, the mass is $2\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}.$\n\n- After $3$ hours, the mass is $2\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{3}.$\n\n- $…$\n\nRepeating this pattern, we see that the mass after $9$ hours is $2\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{9}\\,\\text{kg}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566231 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566231 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61703" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566231 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566231 #edb/ref 1071 "A soccer club started with $120$ members. The number of members in the club then decreased by $\\frac{1}{5}$ every year. Which expression gives approximately the number of members after $3$ years?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566231 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5c6f292d-8813-58fc-b4b8-7f51b18fc102" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566231 #edb/ref 1074 "If the number of members reduced by $\\frac{1}{5}$ every year, it means that $\\frac{4}{5}$ of members remained every year.\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, there were $120\\cdot (\\frac{4}{5})$ members.\n\n- After $2$ years, there were approximately $120\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}$ members.\n\n- After $3$ years, there were approximately $120\\cdot {(\\frac{4}{5})}^{3}$ members." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566251 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566251 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61861" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566251 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566251 #edb/ref 1071 "Nathan invested $\\$5\\,600$ into a company which then went on to lose $7%$ of its value every year. Which expression gives the value of Nathan's investment after $3$ years?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566251 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "92938c74-0d42-5181-8d49-61141e646c18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566251 #edb/ref 1074 "The number $7%$ (expressed as a decimal) is equal to $0.07.$ Therefore, a decrease of $7%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of:\n\n$$\n1-0.07=0.93\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- After $1$ year, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, the value of the investment was $5\\,600\\cdot (0.93)^{3}$ dollars." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566289 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5217ad06-79dc-5267-a1fc-7ac92196ff07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566289 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186566251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566309 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186566289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566309 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c2970b7a-793f-5b1c-9e78-4dd00bd3e750" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566309 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186566231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566316 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186566309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566316 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "df22a5ba-f76c-5c34-9764-841fff0c157d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566316 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186566200 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
